    <div>
      <h2 id="what-title">What AccountOrbit does</h2>
      <p>Finding accounting help usually means choosing between firms, directories and online filing services without a clear view of who does the work or what they are qualified to do.</p>
      <p class="para">AccountOrbit gives you one point of contact. You describe your requirement, such as monthly bookkeeping, a GST return or a reply to a notice, and {{ site.owner.name }} works through it with you: the task, the records involved, the timing and any part the law reserves for a particular qualification. He then coordinates the next steps.</p>
      <p class="para">The site also publishes plain explanations of services, trades and Delhi's business areas, so that you can make a better decision with or without AccountOrbit.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Who runs it, and what it is not</h2>
      <p>AccountOrbit is owned and managed by {{ site.owner.name }}, who runs its day-to-day operations, handles enquiries and speaks with customers himself. Personal profiles: {% ext site.owner.facebook, "Facebook" %} and {% ext site.owner.instagram, "Instagram" %}. These are personal accounts, not AccountOrbit company pages.</p>
      <p class="para">AccountOrbit is not a firm of Chartered Accountants, and no professional qualification is claimed for it or for its owner. Work the law reserves for a qualified professional must be done and signed by someone who holds that qualification. Only facts about the owner that are confirmed for publication appear on this site.</p>
      <p class="para">Deepak describes his own role on the <a href="/about-me/">About Deepak Mittal</a> page.</p>
      {% gap "the operating entity." %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

